# The index already stores every text file as LF, but Windows checkouts with
# core.autocrlf=true turned them into CRLF. That split is invisible until an
# edit or a scripted replacement misses: a `.Replace()` written with "\n" hits
# nothing in a CRLF file and reports no error, so a change can silently not
# apply while the test that was supposed to catch it goes on passing.
#
# Pinning the working tree to LF removes the split rather than teaching every
# tool about it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated and vendored, never edited by hand.
app/meltano-source.css -diff linguist-generated
